{"name":"Dodie Yellow","hex":"#fef65b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dodie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A baby's pacifier or soother."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dodie"},{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dodie","blocks":[{"text":"Dorothy Miranda Clark, known mononymously as Dodie, is an English singer, songwriter, author and YouTuber. She has released two studio albums: Build a Problem (2021), which peaked at number 3 on the UK Albums Chart, and Not for Lack of Trying (2025). She has also released four independent extended plays (EPs): Intertwined (2016), You (2017), Human (2019), and Hot Mess (2022), the first three of which charted in the top 40 of the UK Albums Chart. In 2023, she co-founded a band, Fizz, with her friends Orla Gartland, Greta Isaac, and Martin Luke Brown."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Dodie_performing_in_Chicago_in_February_2022_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Dodie_performing_in_Chicago_in_February_2022_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dodie","wikidata":"Q28004050"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow","wikidata":"Q943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Dodie_Clark2.jpg/500px-Dodie_Clark2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Dodie_Clark2.jpg/500px-Dodie_Clark2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dodie in 2016","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADodie_Clark2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/180228_Dodie_Clark_You_Tour_at_Brussels_La_Madeleine.png/500px-180228_Dodie_Clark_You_Tour_at_Brussels_La_Madeleine.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/180228_Dodie_Clark_You_Tour_at_Brussels_La_Madeleine.png/500px-180228_Dodie_Clark_You_Tour_at_Brussels_La_Madeleine.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dodie performing in Brussels, Belgium during her You Tour in 2018","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A180228_Dodie_Clark_You_Tour_at_Brussels_La_Madeleine.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wi